WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TeslaRegionPage at web parity. The web page
(TeslaRegionPage.tsx) is a thin `PageContainer` wrapper — a page title + subtitle, with
`usePageTitle(title)` — around the shared `<RegionSettings />` component
(features/settings/components/RegionSettings.tsx). The native page reproduces that 1:1,
mirroring the already-shipped sibling `TeslaOrdersPage` (the same "thin chrome page hosting
a shared feature-view section in the Account side-nav group" pattern):

  • TeslaRegionPage — a `ScrollView` column with the web `PageContainer` chrome (page title
    + subtitle, leading-aligned, adaptive across regular-width macOS/iPad and compact iPhone)
    above the embedded shared `RegionSettings` panel. `usePageTitle` → `.navigationTitle`.
    No networking / business logic in the view (ADR-004), exactly like the web page which
    has no state of its own.

  • The embedded `RegionSettings` (pre-existing P4 feature view, TeslaSync/feature-views/
    RegionSettings*.swift) owns ALL of the data + every load state through its `@Observable
    RegionSettingsModel` (P1/S8): the globe header (title/subtitle), the "Synced …" timestamp
    + Refresh button, the region-code / Fleet-API-URL two-cell grid (ViewThatFits reflow), and
    the loading (skeleton) / empty (ContentUnavailableView) / error (retry) / data states plus
    the stale/offline freshness axis. The page binds it via `RegionSettingsModel` and a default
    `RegionSettingsSource` seed (production injects the shared-core source over web
    `useTeslaUserRegion` + `useRefreshTeslaRegion`).

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): single leading-aligned `ScrollView` column that fills the regular
macOS/iPad canvas and the compact iPhone width; the embedded panel reflows its two info cells
from two columns to one as width narrows. All page copy resolves from Localizable.xcstrings
with the web key names verbatim (region.title → translation.region.title, region.subtitle →
translation.region.subtitle); zero hardcoded literals. a11y: header combined into one element;
the embedded panel carries per-cell VoiceOver labels + header trait. Dark mode + Dynamic Type +
tokens inherited from the P2 token catalog + P3 components. Units: none on this surface.

Files (new unless noted):
  Sources/Features/Admin/TeslaRegionPage.swift              (view: PageContainer chrome + embedded RegionSettings + previews)
  Sources/Features/Admin/TeslaRegionRouteRegistration.swift (.teslaRegion route registration + sample source seed)
  Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/TeslaRegionRouteRegistrationTests.swift (registration + route-metadata + parser tests)
  Sources/App/AppRoute.swift          (MOD: +.teslaRegion case / pathSegment "tesla-region" / icon "globe" / .account group)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift          (MOD: wire TeslaRegionRouteRegistration into routeHosts)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings  (MOD: +route.teslaRegion "Region & API"; the 2 parity keys
                                        translation.region.title / translation.region.subtitle + the
                                        embedded panel's region.* keys ALREADY existed in the catalog)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json       (MOD: +2 rows page:admin/TeslaRegion 2/2, apple-macos + apple-ios)

Navigation reconciliation: web /tesla-region is a top-level route in the web Integrations
side-nav group (App.tsx L452, next to /tesla-orders). The native app folds it into the .account
group alongside the sibling .teslaRegion → matches .teslaOrders' established mapping. The web nav
label "Region & API" + the globe icon (Layout.tsx L376) map to route.teslaRegion + "globe".
AppRouteParser.parse(path:) matches the kebab pathSegment directly (no alias needed). Reachable
via the Account-group sidebar entry + any /tesla-region deep link, without displacing other pages.

